From 19a8a3cb5c33142020ae2335dff00a8e2f9442f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:34:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] null patch: 72-entity-uuid-index-per-world

The uuid index was one process-wide resource, so bot B could look up bot A's own entity by uuid (Client::entity_by_uuid, entity_id_by_uuid), and a player-info packet to B could write a GameProfile onto A's entity (retroactively_add_game_profile_component). Each bot has its own world since patch 59, so the index now lives in World (entity_by_uuid), written with entity_by_id and removed with it. EntityUuidIndex keeps only the bots' own join entities, written only by handle_start_join_server_event, so the rejoin lookup at join.rs cannot return a copy from another bot's world.

Vanilla: one ClientLevel per connection, so ClientPacketListener#handlePlayerInfoUpdate and Level#getPlayerByUUID reach only entities of that connection.

Test: entity_uuid_per_world (two bots). The packet test fails on the old code (A's profile name became the one B's packet carried).
